<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="266" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Per-stamp ontology writer identity: UAMI, app setting, Dataverse grants, read-back (#2605)</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — cross-project hand-off (2026-11-06, ontology-platform-r1)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs (H2a, H4b, H10, H7b, H13) and Bicep; adds an identity and its Dataverse grants (auth / least privilege).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive identity work across five handlers plus Bicep, with a least-privilege boundary that must not regress (tags auth).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches H7b SecureRecordSetupProcedure.cs and the H7b ProcedureVersion, which S23 just changed; sequential with any H7b work.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>provisioning, provisioning-handler, l2-controlplane, auth, bicep, dataverse, model1-dedicated, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Give every stamp the ontology writer identity the BFF's SignalWriter / DecisionRecordWriter need, so they stop failing closed: a dedicated UAMI on both BFF slots, its client id as an app setting, a customer-BU application user holding exactly the writer grants, all read back before the run completes.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 handlers H2a, H4b, H10, H7b, H13; customer.bicep). Least privilege is the point of this identity.</role>

  <goal>
    A new stamp run ends with: (1) a UAMI `mi-spaarke-{customerId}-{env}-ontology-writer` in the stamp RG, attached to the BFF site
    AND the staging slot next to the stamp UAMI (keyVaultReferenceIdentity stays the stamp UAMI); (2) `Ontology__Writer__ManagedIdentityClientId`
    on both slots equal to that UAMI's client id; (3) a Dataverse application user for it in the customer business unit, holding the
    customer-BU copy of "Spaarke Ontology Service" and NO other role, and a member of exactly the two writer field-security profiles;
    (4) H7b and H13 fail the run when any of that is missing or wrong. ACME's hand-applied equivalent is adopted with no drift.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Source: GitHub #2605 (filed 2026-11-06 with the ontology project). The BFF resolves the writer through
      `OntologyWriterCredentialFactory` (config key `Ontology:Writer:ManagedIdentityClientId`, FR-21: a separate least-privileged UAMI,
      never the BFF runtime identity). No stamp provisions it, so Signal and Decision Record writes fail closed on every stamp.
      S23 (H7b, procedure v6) gives the BFF RUNTIME user the Ontology Service role; that is a different principal and does not satisfy this.
      Role and profile names are in committed solution source (`SpaarkeMaster/Other/FieldSecurityProfiles.xml`, S23's
      `OntologyServiceRoleName`); privilege specifics come from the ontology project and stay out of committed prose (ontology request).
      The second writer profile ships in SpaarkeMaster 1.2.4.0+ (ACME is on 1.2.3.1 until the 1.3.0.0 upgrade): a missing profile is a
      Resumable refusal naming the solution version, not a pass.
      ACME (2026-11-06): the ontology session may hand-apply the Azure half and part of the Dataverse half under the owner's go, using the
      name above; this task's code must adopt those objects (lookup by name / applicationid, add-only).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep (+ regenerated customer.json) — second `modules/uami.bicep` instance; output its clientId</file>
      <file role="modify">infrastructure/bicep/modules/app-service.bicep, modules/app-service-slot.bicep — optional additional UAMI resource ids (default empty, so other callers are unchanged)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/ (H2a output capture — copy how `uami_client_id` is captured)</file>
      <file role="modify">H4b manifest + `PerEnvSourceCatalog.cs` source for `Ontology__Writer__ManagedIdentityClientId` (copy the `Graph__ManagedIdentity__ClientId` entry) + FilePerEnvSettingsManifestTests parity</file>
      <file role="modify">H10 application-user creation (copy the UAMI app-user path: lookup by applicationid, create in the customer BU); record `InterStepState.OntologyWriterSystemUserId`; declare in HandlerRunInputs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SecureRecordSetup/SecureRecordSetupProcedure.cs — new step S24 (canonical reference: S23 in the same file)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SecureRecordSetup/H7bSecureRecordSetupHandler.cs — pass the writer user; ProcedureVersion → 7</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/CustomerIdentityT7Probe.cs — both-slot read-back of the setting (canonical reference: T265's CheckCustomerBusinessUnit)</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md (H2a / H4b / H10 / H7b / T7 rows)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-21 / least privilege">The writer application user holds exactly one role (customer-BU "Spaarke Ontology Service") and exactly the two writer profiles. H10's System Administrator assignment path must NOT apply to it; a test proves it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / T5">Bicep keeps `type: 'UserAssigned'` (never SystemAssigned) and `keyVaultReferenceIdentity` = the stamp UAMI on both slots; `Graph__ManagedIdentity__ClientId` keeps selecting the stamp UAMI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="T261 / G31">The writer UAMI gets NO Graph app role; extend T3's stamp-identity Graph-role check to include it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="run-context contract">Every new InterStepState value has one producer, is declared in HandlerRunInputs, and RunContextContractTests stay green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="H7b idempotency">ProcedureVersion bumps to "secure-setup-procedure=7" with a test that a v6-completed run does not short-circuit past S24 (copy the v5→v6 test).</constraint>
    <constraint source="S24 sweep">Holder sweep: any team or interactive user (null applicationid) holding the customer-BU Ontology Service role copy, or any member of the writer profiles other than the writer user, is QuarantineRequired (copy S23's sweep). Exception: the S23 BFF runtime user is an allowed role holder.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology request">Committed text names identities and profiles but states no privilege specifics and no client ids / object ids.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">No live Azure/Dataverse change and no deploy in this task. ACME application is a separate owner-OK'd action recorded in the T186 run log.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/OntologyWriterCredentialFactory.cs</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds8-uami-dv-appuser-maturity.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Bicep: second UAMI, additional-identity param on the site and slot modules, clientId output; rebuild customer.json; Bicep tests.</step>
    <step order="2">H2a captures the writer clientId; H4b writes `Ontology__Writer__ManagedIdentityClientId` to both slots; manifest parity tests.</step>
    <step order="3">H10 creates or adopts the writer application user in the customer BU (no role assignment from H10); records its systemuserid.</step>
    <step order="4">H7b S24: resolve role copy and both profiles; refuse Resumable when a profile is absent (name the SpaarkeMaster version); sweep; add-only writes; verify read-back fails the run; v7.</step>
    <step order="5">H13 T7: both slots carry the setting equal to the run's writer clientId; T3 includes the writer UAMI.</step>
    <step order="6">Guide rows; dotnet test control-plane tests; one adversarial pass x2 (auth tag).</step>
    <step order="7">TASK-INDEX: `✅ [done]`; notes below.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ontology requires a live Signal-write smoke at H13, STOP: the BFF has no self-test endpoint for it, and adding one is BFF surface owned with ontology (root CLAUDE.md §10/§11). Ask ontology/owner before building it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the writer must live outside the customer BU, or needs a role or profile beyond the three named, STOP and confirm with ontology rather than widening grants.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Stamp UAMI `modules/uami.bicep` (customer.bicep:254), H10's UAMI app-user path, S23 in SecureRecordSetupProcedure.cs, T7's slot read-back.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — every piece extends an existing module or step; no new handler, interface or DI registration. The UAMI is a second instance of the existing module because FR-21 forbids reusing the runtime identity. New members on existing seams (code-review W1, 2026-11-07): IGraphAppRoleParityVerifier.FindAnyRolesAsync — FindUnexpectedRolesAsync deliberately answers Unknown for an empty allowed set, so "allowed = none" needs its own call; ISecureRecordSetupDataverse.ListUserTeamsAsync / ListUserProfilesAsync — the only way to see roles inherited through a team and direct profile memberships, without which S24 cannot prove "exactly this role and these profiles"; TrapVerificationRequest's two writer fields — T7/T3 have no other input.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Every stamp BFF's SignalWriter and DecisionRecordWriter fail closed, so no Signal or Decision Record is ever written on a customer stamp (#2605).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep, modules/app-service.bicep, modules/app-service-slot.bicep, customer.json</output>
    <output type="code">L2 handlers H2a, H4b, H10, H7b (S24), H13 (T7, T3)</output>
    <output type="test">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests (handler, procedure, manifest, run-context tests)</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Bicep emits the writer UAMI and attaches it to site and slot; the stamp UAMI stays the keyVaultReferenceIdentity; callers that pass no extra identities produce unchanged output.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H4b writes the setting to both slots from H2a's output; manifest parity tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H10 creates the writer app user in the customer BU when absent, adopts it when present (no duplicate), and assigns it no role.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">S24 assigns the role and both profile memberships when absent and writes nothing when present; read-back passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: S24 refuses Resumable when a writer profile or the role copy is absent; QuarantineRequired for a human/team holder, an extra profile member, or a writer user outside the customer BU; verify fails when the writer holds any other role.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: T7 fails a slot missing the setting, blank, or different from the run's writer clientId; T3 fails if the writer UAMI holds a Graph role.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A v6-completed run does not short-circuit past S24.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RunContextContractTests and all Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane tests pass. Test scope: the stated contract plus the negatives above; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    <note date="2026-11-07">Done (code + tests + guide; no live change). Commits b514a9edca (bicep/H2a/H4b), fefcfb09b8 (H10 writer App User), 99fb858153 (H7b S24, procedure v7), 77d468dcf7 (H13 T7 + T3), bafbba6a43 (guide), 9073fa3e14 + 3eb0f08a70 + 9f24305bf2 (review fixes). 3315 control-plane tests, ArchTests 1950/1950. The second writer profile ships first in SpaarkeMaster 1.3.0.0 (not 1.2.4.0 as first noted).</note>
    <note date="2026-11-07">Rework (adversarial review x2 — auth): S24 now also refuses a writer that would inherit a role through a team (any team but its unit's default team, or a role on that default team) or holds another profile directly; verify: extras QuarantineRequired, missing Resumable; H10 adoption refuses a row whose azureactivedirectoryobjectid is not the principal id (also the stamp UAMI); H10/H4b say "start a new run" for runs predating an H2a output; privilege specifics dropped from comments. Seeding proofs: team guard 3 tests, profile guard 1, verify class 2, adoption guard 2. Known limits: K4 FindAnyRoles/FindUnexpectedRoles share ~15 lines; S24 inline in RunAsync; H10 checks the writer's unit only at adoption (ordering, no wrong outcome).</note>
    <note date="2026-11-07">Scoped re-check of the fix diff (Sonnet, one pass — the approach did not change): F2 the guide's external-access row asks for a contact role on the customer unit's default team, which S24 refuses (the writer inherits it) — cross-project security decision filed as #2618, S24 left fail-closed, both guide places cross-reference it; K1 late-role test fixed; K2 real Dataverse returning the default team in teammembership_association unconfirmed live (if it does not, no inheritance through it exists either).</note>
    <note date="2026-11-06">Created from #2605 (ontology confirmed stamps must write Signals / Decision Records; owner direction relayed by ontology to add it here). ACME facts sent to ontology the same day; ACME lacks the second writer profile until SpaarkeMaster ≥ 1.2.4.0.</note>
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
